^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-20 17:06] observe — current docs describe the boundary repeatedly, but the CLI lacks the promised roots command and developers must infer how tree selection, query, and editor navigation fit together.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:07] observe — LSP already parses workspace roots, VS Code already indexes annotations, and CLI already selects AST nodes; the missing value is shared root truth and a small composition surface.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:08] decide — implement pure root declaration parsing in seed, filesystem discovery/tree projection in CLI, and a thin VS Code QuickPick over roots and indexed annotations.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:09] taste — the workbench behaves as an organelle by routing intent through specialized machinery without claiming authority over the containing repository.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:11] revise — use organelle as the governing metaphor: the mount is bounded, replaceable machinery within a larger living repository, not its governing center.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:28] implement — shared seed root parsing now serves LSP and CLI; roots and bounded tree commands preserve consumer-relative output and exclude mounted infrastructure by default.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:29] observe — npm prefix execution changes the process directory, so query and select must resolve relative inputs through discovered consumer authority rather than process.cwd.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:30] implement — scaffold and public READMEs now make the prompt contract executable; VS Code exposes one searchable root-and-landmark navigator over LSP-owned data.
 >>[2026-07-20 17:31] verify — TypeScript build, 223 seed tests, mounted workspace tests, LSP workspace tests, canonical roots/tree/select smoke commands, and VS Code bundle pass.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:34] revise — the earlier governing-organelle entry remains historical; bounded mounted instrument is now the neutral contract, with organelle available only as an optional translation profile.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:21] verify — shared root parsing, mount-safe roots/tree/select navigation, prompt references, and editor landmarks are landed; organelle remains an optional explanatory profile rather than active implementation direction.
}

